     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On 23 May 2017, at 13.06, Christoph Helm &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">christop...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Hi Mikko,<span> </span><br><br>Many thanks for your helpful inforamtion on how to specifiy reflective and formative models! Your are right, I mixed up the terms.<span> </span><br><br>As far as I know it is now possible to do multilevel sem in lavaan:<span> </span><a href=\"http://www.educational-measurement.uni-jena.de/Events/Spring+School+2017/Workshops/Workshop+5_+Yves+Rosseel.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.educational-measurement.uni-jena.de/Events/Spring%2BSchool%2B2017/Workshops/Workshop%2B5_%2BYves%2BRosseel.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166743000&amp;usg=AOvVaw02AQN8jt0I2qUNvSoj2f8g\">http://www.educational-measurement.uni-jena.de/Events/Spring+School+2017/Workshops/Workshop+5_+Yves+Rosseel.html</a><span> </span><br></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
