     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><div><br></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br>Best,<span> </span><br>Christoph<span> </span><br><br>Am Dienstag, 23. Mai 2017 08:25:20 UTC+2 schrieb Mikko Rönkkö:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi,<div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On 23 May 2017, at 9.15, Christoph Helm &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">christop...@</a><a href=\"http://gmail.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gmail.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166743000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_BQGgX6shY90JjiPsYWTy\">gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everyone,<span> </span><br><br>I just tried to do my first formative construct with lavaan using the following code:<span> </span><br><br>myMLmodel &lt;- &#39;level: 1<br>         <span> </span>fw =~ a*V2 + b*V3 + d*V4 + e*V5<span> </span><br>         <span> </span>level: 2<br>         <span> </span>fb =~ f*V2 + g*V3 + h*V4 + i*V5 &#39;<br>fit &lt;- sem(myMLmodel, myData, cluster = &quot;V1&quot;, estimator = &quot;MLR&quot;)<br>summary(fit, fit.measures = TRUE, standardized = TRUE)<br></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div>Two problems:</div><div><br></div><div>1) You have specified a factor model, not a formative model. See<span> </span><a href=\"https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/154588/how-to-use-formative-indicators-in-covariance-based-sem-with-lavaan\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/154588/how-to-use-formative-indicators-in-covariance-based-sem-with-lavaan&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166743000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0A1u2H616OPLgwXl9z6h10\">https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/154588/how-to-use-formative-indicators-in-covariance-based-sem-with-lavaan</a></div><div><br></div><div>2) As far as I know, lavaan does not yet support multilevel SEM. Please correct me if this is outdated information.</div><div><br></div><div>Mikko</div><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Model estimation terminated normally and the results (N par, estimates as well as model fit indices such as BIC and AIC) are identically to Mplus output - accept that:<span> </span><br><br>a) no CFI and TLI are reported<span> </span><br>b) SRMR are weird: 1.457 (compared to the Mplus one: .024 within /.009 between)<br>c) RSMEA is slightly higher than in Mplus (.086 vs. .064).<span> </span><br><br>Additionally, I get the following warning, which might be de reason for the issues above:<span> </span><br><br><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:12.499999046325684px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Warning message:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">In pchisq(XX2, df = df2, ncp = ncp) :</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> NaNs wurden erzeugt</span></pre><br>What do I miss here? Many thanks for your support!<br><br>Best, Christoph<span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"></span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"></span><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:12.499999046325684px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><br></pre></div><div><br></div>--<span> </span><br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to<span> </span><a rel=\"nofollow\">lavaan+un...@</a><a href=\"http://googlegroups.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://googlegroups.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166743000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3VzU5vw_i30Ed0lZTotpDY\">googlegroups.com</a>.<br>To post to this group, send email to<span> </span><a rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@</a><a href=\"http://googlegroups.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://googlegroups.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166743000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3VzU5vw_i30Ed0lZTotpDY\">googlegroups.com</a>.<br>Visit this group at<span> </span><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166743000&amp;usg=AOvVaw243nhCx_qAgD9OeYodg1IJ\">https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan</a>.<br>For more options, visit<span> </span><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166743000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0nfLJqfW2Nc2_B25DV_phC\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br></div></blockquote></div><br></div></div></blockquote></div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;wo