   "subject": "Re: CFI and TLI are not reprorted - Warning: In pchisq(XX2, df = df2, ncp = ncp) : NaNs wurden erzeugt",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I met Yves Rosseel at the aforementioned spring school and he supplied me with slides of his seminar. Unfortunately, I did not attend his seminar. Due to copyright I do not know if I can post the slides here, but I guess Yves will be happy to share all slides with you - as he did with me (just drop him an e-mail). <br><br>Maybe you are right and the package is still under developement. I might contact Yves regarding the warning message. <br></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Many thanks for your support!<br><br>Best, Christoph<br><br><br><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Am Dienstag, 23. Mai 2017 12:23:11 UTC+2 schrieb Mikko Rönkkö:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi,<div><br></div><div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On 23 May 2017, at 13.06, Christoph Helm &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">christop...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Hi Mikko,<span> </span><br><br>Many thanks for your helpful inforamtion on how to specifiy reflective and formative models! Your are right, I mixed up the terms.<span> </span><br><br>As far as I know it is now possible to do multilevel sem in lavaan:<span> </span><a href=\"http://www.educational-measurement.uni-jena.de/Events/Spring+School+2017/Workshops/Workshop+5_+Yves+Rosseel.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.educational-measurement.uni-jena.de/Events/Spring%2BSchool%2B2017/Workshops/Workshop%2B5_%2BYves%2BRosseel.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166747000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3wtt0Uu2xLaXrK4bkZKplR\">http://www.educational-measurement.uni-jena.de/Events/Spring+School+2017/Workshops/Workshop+5_+Yves+Rosseel.html</a><span> </span><br></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div>Interesting.</div><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br>However, I can&#39;t find much information on multilevel sem on the lavaan project platform.<span> </span><br></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>The documentation of the current development version (<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.333333015441895px;text-align:center\">0.6-1.1131) says that the cluster argument is not currently used:</span></div><div><br></div><table summary=\"R argblock\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.333333015441895px\"><tbody><tr valign=\"top\"><td style=\"font-size:10pt;min-width:24px;padding-right:12px\"><code>cluster</code></td><td style=\"font-size:10pt\"><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:6px\">Not used yet.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><div><br></div><div>and the model syntax description does not explain the specification of the levels. I assume that these features are still in development.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>How did you know how to specify levels in the model syntax?</div><div><br></div><div>Mikko</div><div><br></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br>Best,<span> </span><br>Christoph<span> </span><br><br>Am Dienstag, 23. Mai 2017 08:25:20 UTC+2 schrieb Mikko Rönkkö:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi,<div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On 23 May 2017, at 9.15, Christoph Helm &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">christop...@</a><a href=\"http://gmail.com/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gmail.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166747000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0GcxN-bf2muoYuIAOFQ4VU\">gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everyone,<span> </span><br><br>I just tried to do my first formative construct with lavaan using the following code:<span> </span><br><br>myMLmodel &lt;- &#39;level: 1<br>         <span> </span>fw =~ a*V2 + b*V3 + d*V4 + e*V5<span> </span><br>         <span> </span>level: 2<br>         <span> </span>fb =~ f*V2 + g*V3 + h*V4 + i*V5 &#39;<br>fit &lt;- sem(myMLmodel, myData, cluster = &quot;V1&quot;, estimator = &quot;MLR&quot;)<br>summary(fit, fit.measures = TRUE, standardized = TRUE)<br></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div>Two problems:</div><div><br></div><div>1) You have specified a factor model, not a formative model. See<span> </span><a href=\"https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/154588/how-to-use-formative-indicators-in-covariance-based-sem-with-lavaan\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/154588/how-to-use-formative-indicators-in-covariance-based-sem-with-lavaan&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166747000&amp;usg=AOvVaw145bliN5s5kju8qEH8wfFB\">https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/154588/how-to-use-formative-indicators-in-covariance-based-sem-with-lavaan</a></div><div><br></div><div>2) As far as I know, lavaan does not yet support multilevel SEM. Please correct me if this is outdated information.</div><div><br></div><div>Mikko</div><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Model estimation terminated normally and the results (N par, estimates as well as model fit indices such as BIC and AIC) are identically to Mplus output - accept that:<span> </span><br><br>a) no CFI and TLI are reported<span> </span><br>b) SRMR are weird: 1.457 (compared to the Mplus one: .024 within /.009 between)<br>c) RSMEA is slightly higher than in Mplus (.086 vs. .064).<span> </span><br><br>Additionally, I get the following warning, which might be de reason for the issues above:<span> </span><br><br><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:12.499999046325684px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Warning message:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">In pchisq(XX2, df = df2, ncp = ncp) :</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> NaNs wurden erzeugt</span></pre><br>What do I miss here? Many thanks for your support!<br><br>Best, Christoph<span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"></span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"></span><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:12.499999046325684px;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><br></pre></div><div><br></div>--<span> </span><br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to<span> </span><a rel=\"nofollow\">lavaan+un...@</a><a href=\"http://googlegroups.com/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://googlegroups.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166747000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ePZokf0fC6Gr1ERFQsEFv\">googlegroups.com</a>.<br>To post to this group, send email to<span> </span><a rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@</a><a href=\"http://googlegroups.com/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://googlegroups.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427166747000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ePZokf0fC6Gr1ERFQsEFv\">googlegroups.com</a>.<br>Visit this group at<span> </span><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan&amp;source=gmail&amp;